  "dimensions": [
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_05b35178",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: obama_vote_for_me_kfc_koolaid_watermelon; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The image features a smiling Barack Obama with overlaid text that reads 'vote for me' and 'free kfc, grape kool aid, & watermelon.' This juxtaposition maps the image of a respected political figure onto a set of racially coded food stereotypes historically associated with Black Americans — particularly the 'watermelon and fried chicken' trope. This trope is a harmful and derogatory stereotype rooted in racist caricatures that reduce Black people to their consumption of specific foods, implying laziness, dependency, or cultural inferiority. The meme's intent is to mock or trivialize Obama's political campaign by invoking these offensive stereotypes, thereby potentially inciting racial resentment or reinforcing harmful biases. While not overtly abusive or hateful toward a specific individual, it leverages racist imagery to undermine the legitimacy of his candidacy or to entertain through a demeaning lens, making it a harmful meme that perpetuates racial stereotypes and can contribute to a hostile environment for Black individuals.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_e56ef87b"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
